Z||000000||jch82||03-27-2001||06:36 PM||||For all those that know about the 3.1 swap....What cars can I get the 3.1 engine out of that will fit in an 85GT. I might be getting this 85GT really soon and my uncle has a low mileage 3.1 (the make and model of the car has slipped my mind) along with a 2.8 (if it runs). I was wondering what the performance gains are from the 2.8 to the 3.1? Any other info on the swap would be greatly appreciated.<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||shain||03-28-2001||05:15 AM||||grab one from a Z24 ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Chris McDonald||03-28-2001||04:29 PM||||Any front wheel drive 3.1 from Lumina van to Z24 will fit.  You will have to plug or retain the crank sensor as you will be using the stock Fiero Distributor.  Make sure you get the flywheel with the 3.1 as well.  They are balanced different.<P>If you get one from a Camaro or Firebird it will not work.  The starter mounting is on the wrong side.  <P>It is tempting, but you can't use the aluminum heads on the Z24, Lumina, Grand Prix etc.  The intake ports are in the wrong place.  I threw away a dozen of them a few years ago after thinking I had found a Fiero gold mine.<P>Good luck.<P>It will have a little more performance.  However, unless you pump it up with other parts, the only way you may know will by on a dyno.||||reg||1
Z||000003||jch82||03-29-2001||07:07 PM||||I know Roger Garrison has a 3.1L with a turbo in his car. Does anyone know what a turbo costs? How reliable are they and do they hurt the engine at all?  Thanks<P>Josh<P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000004||rogergarrison||03-29-2001||08:57 PM||||mine came out of a wrecked Z24. I think if you get one out of a van, the cam will be a little more bottom end torque. I bought a complete turbo kit on Ebay for $1500 I think. sold at the time for around $3000. Dont know whats out there now-but get a kit not just a turbo and try to mickey mouse it or you will blow it up. I have the 410 4 speed, so its pretty torquee clear up to 7000 rpm.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||ironhedno3||03-30-2001||07:17 PM||||the easiest thing to do is use an ironhead 3.1 from a 91-93 lumina apv van..you will need a neutral balance flexplate...if your car is an automatic just knock off the counterweight..by using this engine it is a direct bolt in and will look like a fiero 2.8..the z24 engine is an aluminum head version and will require more work to get in..stock fiero computer and injectors work fine ||||reg||6
Z||000006||LottaBallsCamaro||03-30-2001||10:05 PM||||I haver a 91 lumina 3.1 with 275,000 mi. and counting. I run it right up to the 6,000RPM shift limit everytime I accelerate and I've also ran it down quite a few dirt roads through mud puddles and all that fun stuff. Yet to die...<P>------------------<BR>91'RS 305TBI no mods to date<BR>92' Lumina 275,000 miles and still humping!!!!||||reg||1
